# Garden sources — the codebases the agent can explore.
#
# Each folder listed here is snapshotted (filtered to source/text files under a
# size cap, with VCS/build/env directories skipped) into the agent's read-only
# /garden/projects/<name>. Edit this list to taste, then rebuild:
#
#   python scripts/build_garden.py
#   docker compose build
#
# Syntax:
#   /abs/path/to/project          included as project "<basename>"
#   ~/relative/to/home            ~ and $VARS are expanded
#   myname = ~/some/long/path     override the project name with "myname ="
#   # lines starting with # are comments; blank lines are ignored
#
# Copy this file to garden_sources.txt (gitignored) and edit it. You can also
# pass folders straight to the script (python scripts/build_garden.py ~/a ~/b)
# or point $GARDEN_SOURCES at a different list.
#
# If a listed folder is itself an Aurora harness, its containment files
# (proxy/diode/Dockerfiles/compose/docs/etc.) are redacted from the snapshot
# automatically, so the world never hands the agent a map of its own enclosure.

# Examples — uncomment and replace with your own:
# ~/my-library
# ~/another-project
# notes = ~/writing/notes
